.TH DRIFTWHY 1
.SH NAME
driftwhy \\- capture a file-content drift fingerprint
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B driftwhy
driftwhy --path FILE [--format json]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Produces a current content observation for later comparison; it does not alter the inspected file.
.SH OPTIONS
Use \fBdriftwhy --help\fR for the complete, version-specific flag list.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Uses the shared CLI status convention: 0 success, 1 a completed negative finding or policy failure, 2 invalid usage, 3 a partial result, and 4 a runtime failure. Not every status applies to every command.
